From af5bda369e980a94772a9ed787d7d9af65588088 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 06:50:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] windowing/gbm: the frame that marks the end of Dolby Vision
 goes out in the mode on the output

With video/dveos on (advancedsettings.xml, off by default), native output is left with one more
transport frame, black, whose metadata packets have EOS set, before the restoration
(EndDVBridge(), PresentDVEndOfStream()). Where the restoration goes out in one commit with the mode
that Kodi sets next (SetFullScreen()), that mode was selected (CDRMUtils::SetMode()) before
EndDVBridge() presented the frame: the frame was checked against the next mode, and committed with
what the plane takes of the next resolution.

- At 119.88 or 120 Hz, or in any other mode that does not carry the transport, FlipDVBridgePage()
  found the frame not valid and committed no buffer: the frame never went out, and
  FlipPageTransactional(nullptr) ended the request that was queued (FinishRequest(false): what Kodi
  had queued before it, and what the subsystems told of the lost display queued, was dropped), and
  counted as a failure of native output in the log.
- With a change of mode pending in Kodi (CDVModeMove: a mode that native output moved into and that
  no frame carried yet), the frame carried that modeset itself, and the restoration a second one:
  two changes of the link, which the single commit is there to avoid.
- A resolution of another size than the window would have put the frame on the plane scaled
  (DVModeChangeJoins() wants a resolution of the window's size, so not through it today).

Now SetFullScreen() sends the frame first, where it is wanted (DVEndOfStreamWanted(): the condition
that EndDVBridge() had written in it), as the last frame of the transport in the mode on the output,
before the other subsystems are told of the change and before the next mode is selected;
EndDVBridge() does not send it again (m_dvEndOfStreamSent). And PresentDVEndOfStream() asks first
whether the frame can go out as a transport frame does, without a modeset, in the mode on the output
(CWinSystemGbm::DVEndOfStreamUnfit(), DVBRIDGE::EndOfStreamUnfit(): the selected mode is the one on
the output with no modeset pending, a mode of the transport, and the window and what the plane takes
of it are of the transport's size). Where it cannot, nothing is drawn, swapped or committed, the
request stays as it is, and the log says why ("... left without the frame that marks the end of the
signal (video/dveos): a change of mode is pending, which it would go out with; the output is
restored as it is without it"). CDRMUtils::GetResolutionWidth() and GetResolutionHeight() give the
size that a commit takes of a buffer on the plane.

With video/dveos off, the default, nothing changes: FlipDVBridgePage() is the same, character for
character, and EndDVBridge() and SetFullScreen() are the functions before but for the lines of the
frame, which that condition guards. The restoration in one commit with the next mode, as it was
validated on hardware, is as before.

Checked on the host, with AddressSanitizer and UBSan: the joined branch of SetFullScreen(),
PresentDVEndOfStream(), DVEndOfStreamWanted() and DVEndOfStreamUnfit() as the tree has them, run on a
model of EndDVBridge(), FlipDVBridgePage() and the DRM state (the test checks that the tree still
has what it models): 40 checks pass; on the tree before, 17 fail (at 119.88 and 120 Hz the frame
never sent and the request dropped, at 60 Hz the frame drawn after the next mode was selected, with
a move pending two modesets, a plane of another size). With the setting off, and for a restoration
that does not go with a change of mode, the events are the same before and after. 11 of 11
mutations of the change are noticed. Not seen on a display.
---
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVEndOfStream.h            | 47 +++++++++++++++++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp           | 17 +++++++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h             |  4 ++
 .../windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp | 37 +++++++++++----
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h  |  3 ++
 xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMUtils.h             |  4 ++
 6 files changed, 102 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVEndOfStream.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVEndOfStream.h
index 3a8dabe..affebe5 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVEndOfStream.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/DVEndOfStream.h
@@ -27,4 +27,51 @@ constexpr bool EndOfStreamFrame(bool setting, bool transportLive, bool lowLatenc
 {
   return setting && transportLive && !lowLatency && !sentAlready;
 }
+
+//! Hades: the output as the frame that marks the end of the signal would go out on it
+//! (EndOfStreamUnfit())
+struct EndOfStreamOutput
+{
+  //! the selected mode is the one on the output, with no modeset pending
+  //! (CDRMAtomic::IsSelectedModeCommitted())
+  bool modeOnOutput = false;
+  //! that mode carries the transport (DVBRIDGE::IsTransportMode())
+  bool transportMode = false;
+  int windowWidth = 0; //!< the window that the frame is drawn into
+  int windowHeight = 0;
+  //! what a commit takes of the window on the plane: the size of the resolution that was selected
+  //! with the mode (CDRMUtils::SetMode())
+  int sourceWidth = 0;
+  int sourceHeight = 0;
+};
+
+/*!
+ * \brief Hades: what keeps the frame that marks the end of the signal from going out as one more
+ *        frame of the transport in the mode on the output; nullptr where nothing does
+ *
+ * It is drawn into the window and committed as the transport frames between the first and the
+ * last one are, without a modeset (CWinSystemGbm::FlipDVBridgePage()): the mode that the commit
+ * names has to be the one on the output, a mode of the transport, and the plane has to take the
+ * window whole, at the size of the transport. Asked before anything is drawn: where it would not
+ * go out, nothing is drawn, swapped or committed, and the request that Kodi has queued for the next
+ * commit stays as it is (a commit of no buffer ends it unsent: CDRMAtomic::FlipPageTransactional()).
+ * Where the restoration goes out with the mode that Kodi sets next, the frame goes before
+ * that mode is selected (CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::SetFullScreen()): asked after it, it would be
+ * asked of that mode and of what the plane takes of its resolution, and at 119.88 or 120 Hz, or
+ * in any other mode that does not carry the transport, it would never go out.
+ */
+constexpr const char* EndOfStreamUnfit(const EndOfStreamOutput& out,
+                                       int transportWidth,
+                                       int transportHeight)
+{
+  if (!out.modeOnOutput)
+    return "a change of mode is pending, which it would go out with";
+  if (!out.transportMode)
+    return "the mode on the output does not carry the transport";
+  if (out.windowWidth != transportWidth || out.windowHeight != transportHeight)
+    return "the window is not of the size of the transport";
+  if (out.sourceWidth != transportWidth || out.sourceHeight != transportHeight)
+    return "the plane would take another part of the window than the transport";
+  return nullptr;
+}
 } // namespace DVBRIDGE
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
index 00d8896..624833b 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.cpp
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 #include "drm/DRMWake.h"
 #include "drm/DVBridgeLink.h"
 #ifdef HAVE_DVBRIDGE
+#include "DVEndOfStream.h"
 #include "cores/VideoPlayer/DVDCodecs/Video/DVPlaybackPolicy.h"
 #include "drm/DVBridgeRefused.h"
 #include "drm/DVBridgeState.h"
@@ -1830,6 +1831,22 @@ bool CWinSystemGbm::CheckDisplayChange(bool& another)
   return back || dvChanged;
 }
 
+const char* CWinSystemGbm::DVEndOfStreamUnfit() const
+{
+  const auto drm = std::dynamic_pointer_cast<CDRMAtomic>(m_DRM);
+  const drmModeModeInfo* mode = drm ? drm->GetSelectedMode() : nullptr;
+  if (!mode)
+    return "there is no mode of an atomic output";
+  DVBRIDGE::EndOfStreamOutput out;
+  out.modeOnOutput = drm->IsSelectedModeCommitted();
+  out.transportMode = IsDVTransportMode(*mode);
+  out.windowWidth = m_nWidth;
+  out.windowHeight = m_nHeight;
+  out.sourceWidth = drm->GetResolutionWidth();
+  out.sourceHeight = drm->GetResolutionHeight();
+  return DVBRIDGE::EndOfStreamUnfit(out, DVBRIDGE::TRANSPORT_WIDTH, DVBRIDGE::TRANSPORT_HEIGHT);
+}
+
 bool CWinSystemGbm::FlipDVBridgePage(CDVBridgeState& state,
                                      bool restore,
                                      DVFlip* flip,
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h
index f5dee33..b7c9087 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbm.h
@@ -111,6 +111,10 @@ public:
   //! is kept on the screen where no vblank can (video/dvkeepbycommit). False when it was refused,
   //! or there is no such frame.
   bool FlipDVBridgeAgain(CDVBridgeState& state);
+  //! Hades: what keeps a transport frame from going out in the mode on the output without a
+  //! modeset, as FlipDVBridgePage() commits one, asked before it is drawn
+  //! (DVBRIDGE::EndOfStreamUnfit()); nullptr where nothing does
+  const char* DVEndOfStreamUnfit() const;
   //! Hades: native Dolby Vision can be left with res, the mode that Kodi sets next, in one commit
   //! (see FlipDVBridgePage()), with every backend (CModeChangeHold::DVRestoreJoins()): the output
   //! is captured for native output and on, and res is another mode of the size of the window, not
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
index 18a2728..0ae6261 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.cpp
@@ -274,6 +274,15 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::SetFullScreen(bool fullScreen,
   const drmModeModeInfo* before = nullptr;
   if ((m_dvEndDeferred || m_dvMovePending) && DVModeChangeJoins(m_dvState, res))
   {
+    // Hades: the frame that marks the end of the signal (video/dveos, off by default) goes first,
+    // as the last frame of the transport, in the mode on the output: once the mode of res is
+    // selected below, it would be checked against that mode, and committed with what the plane
+    // takes of res (PresentDVEndOfStream(), DVBRIDGE::EndOfStreamUnfit())
+    if (DVEndOfStreamWanted())
+    {
+      WaitDVBridgeFlip();
+      PresentDVEndOfStream();
+    }
     OnLostDevice();
     m_displayLostSent = true;
     before = m_DRM->GetSelectedMode();
@@ -3430,16 +3439,27 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::DestroyWindow()
   return CWinSystemGbmEGLContext::DestroyWindow();
 }
 
+bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::DVEndOfStreamWanted() const
+{
+  const auto component = CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent();
+  const auto advanced = component ? component->GetAdvancedSettings() : nullptr;
+  return DVBRIDGE::EndOfStreamFrame(advanced && advanced->m_videoDVEndOfStream,
+                                    m_dvState.TransportLive(),
+                                    m_dvBridge && m_dvBridge->LowLatency(), m_dvEndOfStreamSent);
+}
+
 void CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::PresentDVEndOfStream()
 {
   // (once for the restoration that follows: not again when it is refused and tried again)
   m_dvEndOfStreamSent = true;
   unsigned int packets = 0;
-  const char* why = nullptr;
+  // Hades: checked against the mode on the output, and against what a commit takes of the window,
+  // before anything is drawn: a frame that would not go out as a frame of the transport is not
+  // drawn, swapped or committed, and the request that Kodi has queued stays as it is
+  // (DVBRIDGE::EndOfStreamUnfit())
+  const char* why = !m_dvBridge ? "there is no bridge" : DVEndOfStreamUnfit();
   bool shown = false;
-  if (!m_dvBridge)
-    why = "there is no bridge";
-  else if (m_dvBridge->DrawEndOfStream(0, m_nWidth, m_nHeight, true, packets, why))
+  if (!why && m_dvBridge->DrawEndOfStream(0, m_nWidth, m_nHeight, true, packets, why))
   {
     // a transport frame like the others, in a commit that waits for its flip; the restoration
     // follows it
@@ -3499,12 +3519,9 @@ bool CWinSystemGbmGLESContext::EndDVBridge(bool tellModeset, bool withMode)
     // then.
     WaitDVBridgeFlip();
     // Hades: the end of the signal marked first by one more transport frame, as a comparison for a
-    // display (video/dveos, off: DVBRIDGE::EndOfStreamFrame())
-    const auto component = CServiceBroker::GetSettingsComponent();
-    const auto advanced = component ? component->GetAdvancedSettings() : nullptr;
-    if (DVBRIDGE::EndOfStreamFrame(advanced && advanced->m_videoDVEndOfStream,
-                                   m_dvState.TransportLive(),
-                                   m_dvBridge && m_dvBridge->LowLatency(), m_dvEndOfStreamSent))
+    // display (video/dveos, off: DVBRIDGE::EndOfStreamFrame()). Where the restoration goes out with
+    // the mode that Kodi sets next, SetFullScreen() sent it before that mode was selected.
+    if (DVEndOfStreamWanted())
       PresentDVEndOfStream();
     // Restore signaling with a clean ordinary framebuffer, never tunnel pixels.
     glBindFramebuffer(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, 0);
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h
index ee1ad8c..1cd0046 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/WinSystemGbmGLESContext.h
@@ -471,6 +471,9 @@ private:
   //! Hades: one more transport frame, black, that marks the end of the signal (video/dveos;
   //! DVBRIDGE::EndOfStreamFrame()), in a commit that waits for its flip; said in the log
   void PresentDVEndOfStream();
+  //! Hades: ... whether that frame goes before the restoration that comes (DVBRIDGE::
+  //! EndOfStreamFrame(): the setting, the transport on the output, not Low-Latency, not sent yet)
+  bool DVEndOfStreamWanted() const;
   CDVBridgeState m_dvState;
   std::atomic<bool> m_dvRendererNative{false};
   std::atomic<bool> m_dvViewKeepsOrdinary{false};
diff --git a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMUtils.h b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMUtils.h
index 41457f9..0feeebc 100644
--- a/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMUtils.h
+++ b/xbmc/windowing/gbm/drm/DRMUtils.h
@@ -96,6 +96,10 @@ public:
   CDRMCrtc* GetCrtc() const { return m_crtc; }
   CDRMConnector* GetConnector() const { return m_connector; }
   const drmModeModeInfo* GetSelectedMode() const { return m_mode; }
+  //! Hades: the size of the resolution that was selected with the mode (SetMode()): what a commit
+  //! takes of its buffer on the plane (SRC_W, SRC_H)
+  int GetResolutionWidth() const { return m_width; }
+  int GetResolutionHeight() const { return m_height; }
   //! Hades: select again a mode of the connector that GetSelectedMode() gave, of the size of the
   //! one selected now (after a SetMode() whose change of mode did not happen)
   void ReselectMode(const drmModeModeInfo* mode);
